//
// The decode (aie2_decode.py) at 2 layers on NPU2: up to 4 tokens per
// dispatch, on-chip lm_head, sampler and feedback, growing KV. Every token,
// its record's seed, the last token's final residual and the whole KV cache
// match the numpy oracle, from an empty cache, across dispatches with the NPU
// idle between them, into the cache's last rows, for a split dispatch,
// sampled, for a prompt in batches, and with every logit tied across two
// GEMV cores' sets (greedy, and sampled from a 4-entry set).
// --synthetic-weights swaps the embedding table and the layers' own weights
// for seeded ones in the same layout. 16 real layers are the nightly
// component check.
// test_kernel_edges.py runs the kernels' rare paths on one core each.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, xrt_python_bindings, xrt_python_ctrl_scratchpad_bo
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 0 | FileCheck --check-prefix=EMPTY %s
// EMPTY: KV cache: PASS
// EMPTY: decode: 4/4 tokens PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 62 --dispatches 2 --idle-s 6 | FileCheck --check-prefix=CARRY %s
// CARRY: KV cache: PASS
// CARRY: decode: 8/8 tokens PASS
// CARRY: carry across 2 dispatches: PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 124 | FileCheck --check-prefix=END %s
// END: KV cache: PASS
// END: decode: 4/4 tokens PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 62 --passes 3 --split | FileCheck --check-prefix=SPLIT %s
// SPLIT: KV cache: PASS
// SPLIT: decode: 3/3 tokens PASS
// SPLIT: 3 tokens vs 3 x 1: PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 5 --sample-temp 0.7 --sample-topk 4 --sample-seed 1234 --dispatches 2 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SAMPLED %s
// SAMPLED: sampler state: PASS
// SAMPLED: sampler state: PASS
// SAMPLED: decode: 8/8 tokens PASS
// SAMPLED: carry across 2 dispatches: PASS
// SAMPLED: sampled draws: 8/8 distinct states PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 60 --prompt-tokens 7 --vs-batch 1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=PROMPT %s
// PROMPT: KV cache: PASS
// PROMPT: decode: 5/5 tokens PASS
// PROMPT: carry across 3 dispatches: PASS
// PROMPT: prompt in batches of 4 vs 1: PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 0 --tied-table | FileCheck --check-prefix=TIED %s
// TIED: KV cache: PASS
// TIED: decode: 4/4 tokens PASS
// TIED: tied table: 4/4 picks are the lower twin PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_decode.py --synthetic-weights --start-pos 5 --kset 4 --sample-temp 0.7 --sample-topk 3 --sample-seed 99 --tied-table | FileCheck --check-prefix=KSET4 %s
// KSET4: sampler state: PASS
// KSET4: decode: 4/4 tokens PASS
// KSET4: sampled draws: 4/4 distinct states PASS
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python %S/test_kernel_edges.py | FileCheck --check-prefix=EDGES %s
// EDGES: mma per-element epilogue: 0 words differ, sums past 2^23, {{.*}}: PASS
// EDGES: mma vector epilogue: 0 words differ, sums within 2^23, {{.*}}: PASS
// EDGES: attention plain: 0 words differ, blocks take ['plain', 'plain'], {{.*}}: PASS
// EDGES: attention dropped rows: 0 words differ, blocks take ['drop', 'plain'], {{.*}}: PASS
// EDGES: attention top of range: 0 words differ, blocks take ['top', 'plain'], {{.*}}: PASS
